-- הסכם קיבוצי מיום 15.5.89 — שכר ותנאי עבודה לעובדים בשירות המעסיקים
-- המדורגים בדרוג עובדי הוראה, לתקופה 1.4.1988 – 31.3.1990: the wage
-- agreement of the 1988–1990 round between the teachers' employers — the
-- State, the Centre of Local Government and the three large cities — and
-- both teachers' unions, הסתדרות המורים and ארגון המורים. Its period and the
-- end of negotiation (§§1–2, 12); a committee on surplus teachers (§3); the
-- waiver of 17,800 role hours (§4); the new salary tables from 1.6.88, 5% and
-- then 10% (§5); fifteen allowances updated (§6): the split allowance, the
-- management and supervision allowances, the academic colleges' principals,
-- the colleges' coordinators, the mother teacher, the preparatory classes,
-- the substitute, physical-education clothing, the Bedouin localities, trips,
-- matriculation preparation, the academic guide, three percentage
-- allowances, the intermediate allowance and the accordion; a mutual-aid
-- fund (§7); the additional retirement track (§8); sabbatical teachers,
-- earlier terms and industrial peace (§§9–11); when it is paid (§13); and
-- the letters of annex ד' (§14).
--
-- THE COPY THE CORPUS HOLDS is the Commissioner of Wages' circular
-- הע/48/89(111) of 21.5.1989, which distributes the agreement as its נספח א'
-- and the salary tables as its נספח ב'. Its letter opens the document; the
-- corpus keeps it in the preamble (its standing decision 20), and its
-- instructions are encoded below beside the agreement's, as the circular's.
-- The agreement calls the salary tables "נספח א' להסכם זה" (§5) and the
-- management and supervision tables "נספח ב'" (§6.2(א)); the circular's own
-- lettering is the other way round for the tables. Annexes ג' (§7) and ד'
-- (§14) are not in the scan.
--
-- WHO CITES IT: takanon §1.11's source note 4 names it for the split
-- allowance. For five classes "the rules existing on its signing" that its
-- §6.1 keeps are חוזר מח/11 of 5.6.1988 (l4/circulars-tnai-sherut), a
-- circular, which an agreement does not import for its own rule
-- (tests.test_namespace): the rule is the case's input here.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT parties
IMPORT conventions
IMPORT vocabulary

-- not weighed against `the Hours of Work and Rest Law`: ‘ש"ש’ here counts
-- weekly teaching hours as the measure of a role, an allowance or a
-- coordinator's load (§§3–4, 6.4, 6.5.3, 6.11), and a trip's night or its
-- end after 16:00 (§6.10) prices an allowance; no rule on a working hour,
-- day or week, nor the pay of an hour the law counts.

-- not weighed against `the Equal Pay Law`: the mother teacher's
-- supplement and completion (§6.5) are benefits in connection with
-- parenthood, which the law's §13 leaves out; they are weighed against the
-- Equal Opportunities Law (convention instruments.equal-pay-teaching).

§ `הסכם קיבוצי — שכר ותנאי עבודה לעובדים בשירות המעסיקים המדורגים בדרוג עובדי הוראה (15.5.1989)`

-- not weighed against `the Equal Opportunities Law`: §6.5's mother-teacher
-- rules are the agreement's own benefit of parenthood, and §6.5.3 lets a
-- kindergarten mother teacher be absent up to three hours if a substitute
-- is found; neither limits whom an employer may hire or promote.

DECLARE `1989 wage agreement action` IS ONE OF
    `agree the retirement of surplus teachers, under 1989`
    `negotiate further over the 1988–1990 wages and terms`
    `recommend a new pay structure for principals and supervisors, under 1989`
    `set the procedures of the kindergarten mother teacher's absence, under 1989`
    `agree the money values of physical-education clothing, under 1989`
    `sign the special agreement on the mutual-aid fund, under 1989`
    `fund the mutual-aid fund of 1989`
    `widen the additional retirement track to 50, under 1989`
    `fund the additional retirement track, under 1989`
    `strike or lock out over a matter the 1989 agreement settled`
    `pay what the 1989 agreement gives`

