-- THE AGREEMENT'S HEAD (preamble/p29–p43)

-- akn:preamble/p29 The circular's handwritten collation number, annex א' page 1; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p30 "הסכם קיבוצי", the agreement's title; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p32 The State, represented by the wages commissioner and the Ministry's deputy director-general; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p33 The Centre of Local Government, for every local authority save the three large cities; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p34 The three large cities (Jerusalem, Tel Aviv-Jaffa, Haifa); no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p35 The employers' short name; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p36 "מצד אחד"; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p37 הסתדרות המורים, its secretary-general and its delegation; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p38 Its short name; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p39 ארגון המורים בבתי הספר העל-יסודיים and its delegation; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p40 Its short name; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p41 "מצד שני"; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p43 The words of agreement that introduce the clauses; no rule.

@ref akn:preamble/p31
`the 1989 wage agreement was signed on` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 15 5 1989

-- The recital: the parties negotiated the wages and terms of the employers'
-- employees in the teaching scale ("עובדי הוראה") for 1.4.1988–31.3.1990.
@ref akn:preamble/p42
DECLARE `1989 wage agreement teacher` HAS
    `in the teaching scale, for the 1989 agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
    `employed by one of the 1989 agreement's employers` IS A BOOLEAN @desc the State, a local authority the Centre of Local Government signed for, or one of the three large cities
    `in a government company, for the 1989 agreement` IS A BOOLEAN

-- The circular's ¶7 takes government companies out.
GIVEN t IS A `1989 wage agreement teacher`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the 1989 wage agreement applies to` t IF
        t's `in the teaching scale, for the 1989 agreement`
    AND t's `employed by one of the 1989 agreement's employers`
    AND NOT t's `in a government company, for the 1989 agreement`

§§ `1–2 המבוא ומיצוי המשא ומתן`

@ref akn:art_1
`the 1989 agreement's preamble is part of it` MEANS TRUE

-- §2: it exhausts the negotiation over the teachers' wages and terms for
-- 1.4.88–31.3.90, and no further negotiation is held for that period.
@ref akn:art_2
`no further negotiation over 1988–1990` MEANS
    PARTY `the teachers' union`
    SHANT `negotiate further over the 1988–1990 wages and terms`

-- akn:art_2/p2 The initials at the page's foot; no rule.
-- akn:art_2/p3 The circular's collation number, annex א' page 2; no rule.

§§ `3 מורים עודפים`

-- A joint committee is set up to agree retirement arrangements for all the
-- "surplus teachers" — paid beyond the approved standard of weekly hours for
-- personal or organisational reasons — but no more than 200, by 31.7.89.
@ref akn:art_3
`the most surplus teachers the 1989 committee retires` MEANS 200
`the 1989 surplus-teachers committee finishes by` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 31 7 1989

`agreeing the surplus teachers' retirement` MEANS
    PARTY `the joint committee`
    MUST  `agree the retirement of surplus teachers, under 1989`

§§ `4 ויתור על הקצאת שעות`

-- From 1.9.89 the teachers give up the allocation of 17,800 weekly hours to
-- role holders set under the Etzioni committee's conclusions and the annex
-- of the special agreement of 16.11.83 (§§2.4 and 10), both outside the
-- corpus.
@ref akn:art_4
`the role hours given up under 1989` MEANS 17800

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the 1989 role-hours allocation is given up on` d IF
    d `is on or after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 1989)

§§ `5 טבלאות השכר`

-- From 1.6.88 the salary tables are those of the agreement's annex א' (the
-- four grids at the end of this file), which include a supplement of 5%
-- from 1.6.88 and its completion to 10% from 1.4.89.
@ref akn:art_5
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the 1989 tables' wage supplement on` d IS
    BRANCH IF d `is on or after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 4 1989) THEN 10%
           IF d `is on or after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 1988) THEN 5%
           OTHERWISE 0

§§ `6 גמולים ותשלומים`

-- akn:art_6 The lead-in ("the parties agree to update allowances and payments as follows"); the items are 6.1–6.15.

-- 6.1: the split allowance, under the conditions in the table and the
-- rules existing when the agreement was signed. The table's rows: 5
-- classes, 2% → 3%; 6–7 classes or 3 institutions, 3% → 5%; 8–10 classes,
-- 4% → 6%; 11+ classes, 4% → 7%. 6.1.5: the first three from 1.4.89, the
-- fourth from 1.9.89; before them the existing rate stands.
@ref akn:art_6__para_6-1 akn:art_6__para_6-1/t1
DECLARE `1989 split band` IS ONE OF
    `five classes, under 1989`
    `six or seven classes or three institutions, under 1989`
    `eight to ten classes, under 1989`
    `eleven classes or more, under 1989`

GIVEN classes IS A NUMBER, institutions IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE `1989 split band`
DECIDE `the 1989 split band of` classes institutions IS
    BRANCH IF classes AT LEAST 11 THEN JUST `eleven classes or more, under 1989`
           IF classes AT LEAST 8 THEN JUST `eight to ten classes, under 1989`
           IF classes AT LEAST 6 OR institutions AT LEAST 3 THEN JUST `six or seven classes or three institutions, under 1989`
           IF classes EQUALS 5 THEN JUST `five classes, under 1989`
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

@ref akn:art_6__para_6-1__subpara_6-1-1 akn:art_6__para_6-1__subpara_6-1-2 akn:art_6__para_6-1__subpara_6-1-3 akn:art_6__para_6-1__subpara_6-1-4
GIVEN b IS A `1989 split band`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the split rate existing before 1989 for` b IS
    CONSIDER b
    WHEN `five classes, under 1989` THEN 2%
    WHEN `six or seven classes or three institutions, under 1989` THEN 3%
    WHEN `eight to ten classes, under 1989` THEN 4%
    WHEN `eleven classes or more, under 1989` THEN 4%

GIVEN b IS A `1989 split band`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the split rate 1989 sets for` b IS
    CONSIDER b
    WHEN `five classes, under 1989` THEN 3%
    WHEN `six or seven classes or three institutions, under 1989` THEN 5%
    WHEN `eight to ten classes, under 1989` THEN 6%
    WHEN `eleven classes or more, under 1989` THEN 7%

@ref akn:art_6__para_6-1__subpara_6-1-5 akn:art_6__para_6-1__subpara_6-1-5/p2
GIVEN b IS A `1989 split band`
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `the new split rate applies from, under 1989,` b IS
    IF b EQUALS `eleven classes or more, under 1989`
    THEN DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 1989
    ELSE DATE_FROM_DMY 1 4 1989

GIVEN d IS A DATE, b IS A `1989 split band`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the 1989 split rate on` d b IS
    IF d `is on or after` (`the new split rate applies from, under 1989,` b)
    THEN `the split rate 1989 sets for` b
    ELSE `the split rate existing before 1989 for` b

-- "בהתאם לכללים הקיימים במעמד חתימת הסכם זה": who is entitled stays as the
-- existing rules had it, and the agreement does not restate them. For five
-- classes they are חוזר מח/11 of 5.6.1988 (a position from 79% to 95% split
-- among 5 classes, in an elementary or post-elementary school), for the
-- other bands rules outside the corpus; either way the case's input. The
-- allowance is a percentage of the full combined salary, as חוזר מח/11
-- takes it.
GIVEN classes IS A NUMBER, institutions IS A NUMBER
      `entitled by the existing rules for its band` IS A BOOLEAN @desc the rules existing on 15.5.89: for five classes חוזר מח/11 of 5.6.1988, otherwise outside the corpus
      `full combined salary` IS A NUMBER
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the split allowance under 1989` classes institutions `entitled by the existing rules for its band` `full combined salary` d IS
    CONSIDER `the 1989 split band of` classes institutions
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST b THEN
        IF `entitled by the existing rules for its band`
        THEN JUST (`the 1989 split rate on` d b TIMES `full combined salary`)
        ELSE JUST 0

-- 6.1.6: those not named above who are paid a split allowance of 3% on the
-- eve of the signing have it raised to 5% from 1.4.89.
@ref akn:art_6__para_6-1__subpara_6-1-6
GIVEN d IS A DATE, `the rate paid on the eve of the signing` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the split rate of one not named in 6.1, under 1989, on` d `the rate paid on the eve of the signing` IS
    IF `the rate paid on the eve of the signing` EQUALS 3% AND d `is on or after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 4 1989)
    THEN 5%
    ELSE `the rate paid on the eve of the signing`

-- 6.2: the management and supervision allowances. (א): a budget of 0.3% of
-- the teachers' pay, carried out by the table of annex ב' below, from
-- 1.4.89. (ב): a joint committee recommends a new pay structure for
-- principals and supervisors within three months.
-- akn:art_6__para_6-2 The heading of 6.2; its items are (א) and (ב).
@ref akn:art_6__para_6-2__subpara_a
`the cost of the 1989 management and supervision allowances` MEANS 0.3%

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the 1989 management table applies on` d IF
    d `is on or after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 4 1989)

@ref akn:art_6__para_6-2__subpara_b
`the 1989 principals' pay committee recommends within, in months` MEANS 3

`recommending the principals' pay structure` MEANS
    PARTY `the joint committee`
    MUST  `recommend a new pay structure for principals and supervisors, under 1989`

-- akn:art_6__para_6-2__subpara_b/p2 The initials at the page's foot; no rule.
-- akn:art_6__para_6-2__subpara_b/p3 The circular's collation number, annex א' page 3; no rule.

-- 6.3: the academic colleges. 6.3.1: the principals of the academic
-- colleges recognised to grant the B.Ed. and listed in 6.3.4 get the
-- management allowance from 1.9.89, instead of that of a teachers'
-- seminary, by seniority in management: 40% in year 1, 2 points a year, 60%
-- from year 11.
-- akn:art_6__para_6-3 The heading of 6.3; its items are 6.3.1–6.3.4.
@ref akn:art_6__para_6-3__subpara_6-3-1 akn:art_6__para_6-3__subpara_6-3-1/t1
GIVEN `year of seniority in management` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `a 1989 college principal's management allowance` `year of seniority in management` IS
    IF `year of seniority in management` LESS THAN 1
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST ((38 PLUS 2 TIMES (min `year of seniority in management` 11)) DIVIDED BY 100)

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the 1989 college principals' allowance applies on` d IF
    d `is on or after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 1989)

-- 6.3.2: every 250 students let a listed college appoint a deputy, up to
-- five. The first gets 75% of the principal's percentage, the second 70%,
-- the third to fifth 65%.
@ref akn:art_6__para_6-3__subpara_6-3-2
GIVEN students IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the deputies a college may appoint under 1989` students IS
    min (TRUNC (students DIVIDED BY 250) 0) 5

@ref akn:art_6__para_6-3__subpara_6-3-2__cls_6-3-2-1 akn:art_6__para_6-3__subpara_6-3-2__cls_6-3-2-2 akn:art_6__para_6-3__subpara_6-3-2__cls_6-3-2-3
GIVEN `which deputy` IS A NUMBER @desc 1 for the first deputy, 2 for the second, 3–5 for the third to the fifth
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `a 1989 college deputy's share of the principal's allowance` `which deputy` IS
    BRANCH IF `which deputy` EQUALS 1 THEN JUST (75%)
           IF `which deputy` EQUALS 2 THEN JUST (70%)
           IF `which deputy` AT LEAST 3 AND `which deputy` AT MOST 5 THEN JUST (65%)
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- 6.3.3: no seniority additions on those percentages; the allowance is
-- computed on the new combined salary of an academic (B.A.) teacher at the
-- top of the seniority and on each teacher's "stay supplement".
@ref akn:art_6__para_6-3__subpara_6-3-3
GIVEN percentage IS A NUMBER
      `B.A. combined salary at the top of the seniority` IS A NUMBER
      `the teacher's stay supplement` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `a 1989 college management allowance` percentage `B.A. combined salary at the top of the seniority` `the teacher's stay supplement` IS
    percentage TIMES (`B.A. combined salary at the top of the seniority` PLUS `the teacher's stay supplement`)

-- 6.3.4: the colleges 6.3.1–6.3.2 apply to.
@ref akn:art_6__para_6-3__subpara_6-3-4 akn:art_6__para_6-3__subpara_6-3-4/p2
`the academic colleges of 1989` MEANS
    LIST "דוד ילין", "הקבוצים", "וינגייט", "בית ברל", "לוינסקי", "מכללת ירושלים לבנות"

-- akn:art_6__para_6-3__subpara_6-3-4/p3 The initials at the page's foot; no rule.
-- akn:art_6__para_6-3__subpara_6-3-4/p4 The circular's collation number, annex א' page 4; no rule.

-- 6.4: in the colleges and teachers' seminaries, teaching employees are
-- appointed coordinators of a track, a stream or a subject, in coordination
-- with the Ministry. 6.4.1: a "track" is the educational layer the student
-- trains for (early childhood, elementary, junior high); a "stream" a
-- special field of study (music, art, creative or special education).
@ref akn:art_6__para_6-4 akn:art_6__para_6-4__subpara_6-4-1 akn:art_6__para_6-4__hc_1/p1 akn:art_6__para_6-4__hc_2/p1
DECLARE `1989 college coordination` IS ONE OF
    `coordinator of a track, under 1989`
    `coordinator of a stream, under 1989`
    `coordinator of a subject, under 1989`

-- 6.4.2: a track or stream coordinator, from 1.9.89, by the number of
-- students times weekly teaching hours: up to 2000 6%, to 4000 7%, to 6000
-- 8%, to 8000 9%, 8001 and more 10%, of the combined salary.
@ref akn:art_6__para_6-4__subpara_6-4-2 akn:art_6__para_6-4__subpara_6-4-2/t1
GIVEN `students times weekly teaching hours` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `a 1989 track or stream coordinator's rate` `students times weekly teaching hours` IS
    BRANCH IF `students times weekly teaching hours` AT MOST 2000 THEN 6%
           IF `students times weekly teaching hours` AT MOST 4000 THEN 7%
           IF `students times weekly teaching hours` AT MOST 6000 THEN 8%
           IF `students times weekly teaching hours` AT MOST 8000 THEN 9%
           OTHERWISE 10%

-- 6.4.3: a subject coordinator in a seminary or college, by the subject's
-- weekly teaching hours: 30–39 6%, 40–49 7%, 50–59 8%, 60–69 9%, 70+ 10%.
-- The table starts at 30 hours and gives nothing below.
@ref akn:art_6__para_6-4__subpara_6-4-3 akn:art_6__para_6-4__subpara_6-4-3/t1
GIVEN `the subject's weekly teaching hours` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `a 1989 subject coordinator's rate` `the subject's weekly teaching hours` IS
    BRANCH IF `the subject's weekly teaching hours` AT LEAST 70 THEN JUST (10%)
           IF `the subject's weekly teaching hours` AT LEAST 60 THEN JUST (9%)
           IF `the subject's weekly teaching hours` AT LEAST 50 THEN JUST (8%)
           IF `the subject's weekly teaching hours` AT LEAST 40 THEN JUST (7%)
           IF `the subject's weekly teaching hours` AT LEAST 30 THEN JUST (6%)
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- 6.4.4: the coordinator is a permanent teaching employee employed at least
-- 2/3 of a position in the seminaries and colleges. 6.4.5: one
-- coordination allowance only.
@ref akn:art_6__para_6-4__subpara_6-4-4
GIVEN permanent IS A BOOLEAN, `position fraction in the seminaries and colleges` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may be appointed a 1989 college coordinator` permanent `position fraction in the seminaries and colleges` IF
    permanent AND `position fraction in the seminaries and colleges` AT LEAST 2 DIVIDED BY 3

@ref akn:art_6__para_6-4__subpara_6-4-5
`the coordination allowances one may hold under 1989` MEANS 1

-- akn:art_6__para_6-4__subpara_6-4-5/p2 The initials at the page's foot; no rule.
-- akn:art_6__para_6-4__subpara_6-4-5/p3 The circular's collation number, annex א' page 5; no rule.

-- 6.5: the mother teacher, from 1.9.89. 6.5.1: employed between 79% and
-- 90% of a position, a supplement of 10% of her combined salary. 6.5.2:
-- between 91% and 100%, completion of her combined salary to a full
-- position. Both ends in (convention thresholds.until); between 90% and 91%
-- the text is silent, and a position there is read with 6.5.2, the band
-- whose floor it passes (convention position.points: a position is read in
-- whole points).
-- akn:art_6__para_6-5 The heading of 6.5; its items are 6.5.1–6.5.3.
@ref akn:art_6__para_6-5__subpara_6-5-1 akn:art_6__para_6-5__subpara_6-5-2
GIVEN `position fraction` IS A NUMBER, `combined salary of a full position` IS A NUMBER, d IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `a 1989 mother teacher's salary` `position fraction` `combined salary of a full position` d IS
    IF NOT d `is on or after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 1989)
    THEN `position fraction` TIMES `combined salary of a full position`
    ELSE BRANCH IF `position fraction` AT LEAST 0.79 AND `position fraction` AT MOST 0.90
                THEN (`position fraction` PLUS 10%) TIMES `combined salary of a full position`
                IF `position fraction` GREATER THAN 0.90 AND `position fraction` AT MOST 1
                THEN `combined salary of a full position`
                OTHERWISE `position fraction` TIMES `combined salary of a full position`

-- 6.5.3: a kindergarten mother teacher in a full position may be absent up
-- to 3 weekly hours if a substitute approved by the supervision is found;
-- phased over five years from 5750 to 5754 inclusive, for a quota of 800
-- kindergarten teachers in 5750; a joint committee sets the procedures.
@ref akn:art_6__para_6-5__subpara_6-5-3
`the weekly hours a 1989 kindergarten mother teacher may be absent` MEANS 3
`the 1989 kindergarten mother teachers' quota in 5750` MEANS 800

GIVEN `full position` IS A BOOLEAN, `an approved substitute is found` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a 1989 kindergarten mother teacher may be absent` `full position` `an approved substitute is found` IF
    `full position` AND `an approved substitute is found`

`setting the kindergarten mother teacher's procedures` MEANS
    PARTY `the joint committee`
    MUST  `set the procedures of the kindergarten mother teacher's absence, under 1989`

-- 6.6: in preparatory classes or "מפתנים", from 1.9.89, a special
-- allowance of 10% of the combined salary instead of the 7% paid until
-- then, and 6.5% instead of 3.5%.
@ref akn:art_6__para_6-6
GIVEN d IS A DATE, `the rate paid until 1.9.89` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the 1989 preparatory-class rate on` d `the rate paid until 1.9.89` IS
    IF NOT d `is on or after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 1989)
    THEN JUST `the rate paid until 1.9.89`
    ELSE BRANCH IF `the rate paid until 1.9.89` EQUALS 7% THEN JUST (10%)
                IF `the rate paid until 1.9.89` EQUALS 3.5% THEN JUST (6.5%)
                OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- 6.7: a substitute from outside the school's staff is paid, from 1.9.89,
-- the combined salary of a senior teacher with three years' seniority and
-- the stay supplement; this cancels the earlier tariff.
@ref akn:art_6__para_6-7
GIVEN `senior teacher's combined salary at three years` IS A NUMBER, `stay supplement` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `a 1989 outside substitute's salary` `senior teacher's combined salary at three years` `stay supplement` IS
    `senior teacher's combined salary at three years` PLUS `stay supplement`

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the 1989 substitute's pay applies on` d IF
    d `is on or after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 1989)

-- 6.8: physical-education clothing: a joint committee agrees the money
-- values by 30.7.89; the cost is at most 500,000 shekels, from 1.9.89, the
-- payment updated by the cost-of-living supplements.
@ref akn:art_6__para_6-8
`the most the 1989 physical-education clothing costs` MEANS 500000
`the 1989 clothing committee finishes by` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 30 7 1989

`agreeing the physical-education clothing` MEANS
    PARTY `the joint committee`
    MUST  `agree the money values of physical-education clothing, under 1989`

-- 6.9: teachers in the Bedouin localities of the south whose family lives
-- permanently outside the Southern District get a rent participation of 90
-- shekels a month for a full position from 1.9.89, updated yearly by the
-- cost-of-living supplements (read pro rata to the position: convention
-- position.above-full).
@ref akn:art_6__para_6-9
GIVEN `family lives outside the Southern District` IS A BOOLEAN, `position fraction` IS A NUMBER, d IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the 1989 Bedouin-locality rent participation` `family lives outside the Southern District` `position fraction` d IS
    IF `family lives outside the Southern District` AND d `is on or after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 1989)
    THEN 90 TIMES `position fraction`
    ELSE 0

-- 6.10: from 1.9.89, a teacher on a trip with a night away gets 35 shekels
-- a day and night; one escorting pupils on trips, journeys or sports
-- contests that end after 16:00 gets 6 shekels from the first day, provided
-- 4 escort days a year were accumulated; updated by the cost of living.
@ref akn:art_6__para_6-10
`the 1989 trip allowance for a day and night` MEANS 35
`the 1989 escort allowance for a day` MEANS 6
`the escort days a year the 1989 allowance needs` MEANS 4

GIVEN `escort days in the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the 1989 escort allowance for the year` `escort days in the year` IS
    IF `escort days in the year` AT LEAST `the escort days a year the 1989 allowance needs`
    THEN `escort days in the year` TIMES `the 1989 escort allowance for a day`
    ELSE 0

-- 6.11: matriculation preparation, from 1.4.89. 6.11.1: by examination
-- units, weekly hours and 2%: 1 unit 1 hour, 2 units 1.5, 3 units 2, 4
-- units 3, 5 or more 3.5, each with 2%.
-- akn:art_6__para_6-11 The heading of 6.11; its items are 6.11.1–6.11.4.
@ref akn:art_6__para_6-11__subpara_6-11-1 akn:art_6__para_6-11__subpara_6-11-1/t1
GIVEN units IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the 1989 matriculation allowance hours for` units IS
    BRANCH IF units AT LEAST 5 THEN JUST 3.5
           IF units EQUALS 4 THEN JUST 3
           IF units EQUALS 3 THEN JUST 2
           IF units EQUALS 2 THEN JUST 1.5
           IF units EQUALS 1 THEN JUST 1
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

`the 1989 matriculation allowance's percentage` MEANS 2%

-- akn:art_6__para_6-11__subpara_6-11-1/p2 The initials at the page's foot; no rule.
-- akn:art_6__para_6-11__subpara_6-11-1/p3 The circular's collation number, annex א' page 6; no rule.

-- 6.11.2: preparing for state final examinations in technological
-- education, or examinations outside the matriculation reform, adds 2% to
-- the existing allowance.
@ref akn:art_6__para_6-11__subpara_6-11-2
`the 1989 addition for technological or non-reform examinations` MEANS 2%

-- 6.11.3: the 2% are taken of the combined salary of a full position by
-- grade and seniority, whatever the part of the position.
@ref akn:art_6__para_6-11__subpara_6-11-3
GIVEN `combined salary of a full position` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the 1989 matriculation percentage allowance` `combined salary of a full position` IS
    `the 1989 matriculation allowance's percentage` TIMES `combined salary of a full position`

-- 6.11.4: from 1.4.89 the arrangement cancels every earlier one.
@ref akn:art_6__para_6-11__subpara_6-11-4
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the 1989 matriculation arrangement governs on` d IF
    d `is on or after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 4 1989)

-- 6.12: a "teacher in a guidance role" with an academic degree and more
-- than two years in the role gets, from 1.9.89, the "mentor teacher
-- allowance" at the rate the supervision table of annex ב' sets for a
-- "guide" — read as the table's "מורה מדריך" column, 31%, the allowance it
-- names (the "מדריך" column is the guides' own).
@ref akn:art_6__para_6-12
GIVEN academic IS A BOOLEAN, `years in the guidance role` IS A NUMBER, d IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the 1989 academic guide's allowance rate` academic `years in the guidance role` d IS
    IF academic AND `years in the guidance role` GREATER THAN 2 AND d `is on or after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 1989)
    THEN `the 1989 mentor teacher's rate`
    ELSE 0

-- 6.13: from 1.4.89 added to the existing percentages: (א) the education
-- allowance 1 point; (ב) a teaching certificate or a double degree 1.5;
-- (ג) a "special allowance" of 1 for budgetary pensioners not entitled to
-- the educator's or the subject-and-training allowance.
@ref akn:art_6__para_6-13
DECLARE `1989 percentage allowance` IS ONE OF
    `the education allowance, under 1989`
    `the teaching-certificate or double-degree allowance, under 1989`
    `the pensioners' special allowance, under 1989`

@ref akn:art_6__para_6-13__subpara_a akn:art_6__para_6-13__subpara_b akn:art_6__para_6-13__subpara_c
GIVEN a IS A `1989 percentage allowance`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the points 1989 adds to` a IS
    CONSIDER a
    WHEN `the education allowance, under 1989` THEN 1%
    WHEN `the teaching-certificate or double-degree allowance, under 1989` THEN 1.5%
    WHEN `the pensioners' special allowance, under 1989` THEN 1%

-- 6.14: the intermediate allowance, 3% of the combined salary, for
-- teachers with a recognised academic degree and certified practical
-- engineers holding a permanent licence or a certificate obtained by
-- external study and examination; limited to 1000 teachers; from 1.4.89;
-- the procedures agreed in the supreme in-service committee.
@ref akn:art_6__para_6-14
`the 1989 intermediate allowance` MEANS 3%
`the teachers the 1989 intermediate allowance is limited to` MEANS 1000

-- 6.15: a teacher who uses a private accordion for work gets 20 shekels a
-- month from 1.4.89, 25 from 1.9.89.
@ref akn:art_6__para_6-15 akn:art_6__para_6-15/p2
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the 1989 accordion allowance on` d IS
    BRANCH IF d `is on or after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 1989) THEN 25
           IF d `is on or after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 4 1989) THEN 20
           OTHERWISE 0

§§ `7 קרן לסיוע הדדי`

-- A fund of 2 million shekels for mutual aid, financed equally by the
-- parties; they sign a special agreement on it (annex ג', not in the
-- corpus).
@ref akn:art_7
`the 1989 mutual-aid fund` MEANS 2000000
`each side's half of the 1989 mutual-aid fund` MEANS `the 1989 mutual-aid fund` DIVIDED BY 2

@ref akn:art_7/p2
`why the 1989 mutual-aid agreement is not here` MEANS
    `the text is missing` "נספח ג' להסכם מיום 15.5.89, ההסכם הקיבוצי המיוחד על הקרן לסיוע הדדי"

`signing the mutual-aid agreement` MEANS
    PARTY `the State`
    MUST  `sign the special agreement on the mutual-aid fund, under 1989`

§§ `8 מסלול פרישה נוסף`

-- The parties continue the additional retirement track of §6 of the
-- agreement of 24.1.88 (outside the corpus). 8.1: no more than 40 retire by
-- it for 5750; 8.2: a joint committee of the wages commissioner, the local
-- government's deputy director-general, the Histadrut's secretary-general
-- and the Irgun's chairman may widen it to 50 in exceptional cases; 8.3:
-- later years' numbers are negotiated; 8.4: the employers fund it through
-- the ק.פ.מ.
@ref akn:art_8
`why the 1988 retirement track is not here` MEANS
    `outside the corpus` "סעיף 6 להסכם מיום 24.1.88"

@ref akn:art_8__para_8-1
`the 1989 additional-retirement quota for 5750` MEANS 40

@ref akn:art_8__para_8-2
`the 1989 additional-retirement quota at most, in exceptional cases` MEANS 50

`widening the additional retirement track` MEANS
    PARTY `the joint committee`
    MAY   `widen the additional retirement track to 50, under 1989`

-- akn:art_8__para_8-2/p2 The initials at the page's foot; no rule.
-- akn:art_8__para_8-2/p3 The circular's collation number, annex א' page 7; no rule.

@ref akn:art_8__para_8-3
`why the 1989 retirement quotas of later years are not here` MEANS
    `set elsewhere` "המשא ומתן שינוהל מעת לעת"

@ref akn:art_8__para_8-4
`funding the additional retirement track` MEANS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `fund the additional retirement track, under 1989`

§§ `9–13 תחולה, תקופה ותשלום`

@ref akn:art_9
`the 1989 agreement applies to teachers on sabbatical from the in-service funds` MEANS TRUE

-- §10: terms set earlier in collective agreements, arrangements or written
-- undertakings stay in force unless this agreement changes them expressly
-- or by implication.
@ref akn:art_10
GIVEN `changed by the 1989 agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an earlier term stays in force under 1989` `changed by the 1989 agreement` IF
    NOT `changed by the 1989 agreement`

-- §11: during the agreement no side strikes, locks out or disrupts work
-- over the matters it settled.
@ref akn:art_11
`industrial peace under the 1989 agreement` MEANS
    (PARTY `the teachers' union`
     SHANT `strike or lock out over a matter the 1989 agreement settled`)
    RAND
    (PARTY `the secondary teachers' organisation`
     SHANT `strike or lock out over a matter the 1989 agreement settled`)
    RAND
    (PARTY `the State`
     SHANT `strike or lock out over a matter the 1989 agreement settled`)

-- §12: the agreement's period is 1.4.1988–31.3.1990, save the clauses that
-- set another date.
@ref akn:art_12
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `in the 1989 wage agreement's period` d IF
        d `is on or after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 4 1988)
    AND d `is on or before` (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 3 1990)

-- §13: the payments are made in the May 1989 salary and no later than June
-- 1989, by each clause's date, the salary advance paid in November 1988
-- set off.
@ref akn:art_13
`the 1989 agreement is paid in the salary of` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 5 1989
`the 1989 agreement is paid no later than the salary of` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 1989

GIVEN `due under the agreement` IS A NUMBER, `the November 1988 advance` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `what 1989 still pays after the advance` `due under the agreement` `the November 1988 advance` IS
    max 0 (`due under the agreement` MINUS `the November 1988 advance`)

`paying the 1989 agreement` MEANS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `pay what the 1989 agreement gives`

