GIVEN t IS A `1989 salary table`
GIVETH A LIST OF LIST OF MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the 1989 cells of` t IS
    CONSIDER t
    WHEN `the 1989 table of 1.6.88` THEN `the cells of the 1989 table of 1.6.88`
    WHEN `the 1989 table of 1.10.88` THEN `the cells of the 1989 table of 1.10.88`
    WHEN `the 1989 table of 1.2.89` THEN `the cells of the 1989 table of 1.2.89`
    WHEN `the 1989 table of 1.4.89` THEN `the cells of the 1989 table of 1.4.89`

-- What each table prints it is in force from: 1.6.88, 1.10.88, 1.2.89 and
-- 1.4.89.
@ref akn:att_1__hc_1/p16 akn:att_1__hc_1/p11 akn:att_1__hc_1/p22 akn:att_1__hc_1/p27
GIVEN t IS A `1989 salary table`
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `the day the 1989 table is in force from` t IS
    CONSIDER t
    WHEN `the 1989 table of 1.6.88` THEN DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 1988
    WHEN `the 1989 table of 1.10.88` THEN DATE_FROM_DMY 1 10 1988
    WHEN `the 1989 table of 1.2.89` THEN DATE_FROM_DMY 1 2 1989
    WHEN `the 1989 table of 1.4.89` THEN DATE_FROM_DMY 1 4 1989

-- The table in force on a day: the latest one whose day has come, within
-- the agreement's period (§12); none before 1.6.88.
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE `1989 salary table`
DECIDE `the 1989 table in force on` d IS
    BRANCH IF NOT `in the 1989 wage agreement's period` d THEN NOTHING
           IF d `is on or after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 4 1989) THEN JUST `the 1989 table of 1.4.89`
           IF d `is on or after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 2 1989) THEN JUST `the 1989 table of 1.2.89`
           IF d `is on or after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 10 1988) THEN JUST `the 1989 table of 1.10.88`
           IF d `is on or after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 1988) THEN JUST `the 1989 table of 1.6.88`
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- A table's cell at a seniority year (1 to 33) and a grade (its place in
-- the header, 1 to 13); NOTHING outside the table or where the scan does
-- not settle the cell.
GIVEN t IS A `1989 salary table`
      `the year of seniority he is in` IS A NUMBER
      grade IS A NUMBER @desc its place among `the grades of the 1989 tables`, from 1
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the cell of the 1989 table` t `the year of seniority he is in` grade IS
    IF     `the year of seniority he is in` AT LEAST 1
       AND `the year of seniority he is in` AT MOST `the seniority rows the 1989 tables print`
       AND grade AT LEAST 1
       AND grade AT MOST count `the grades of the 1989 tables`
    THEN at (at (`the 1989 cells of` t) (`the year of seniority he is in` MINUS 1)) (grade MINUS 1)
    ELSE NOTHING

GIVEN d IS A DATE, `the year of seniority he is in` IS A NUMBER, grade IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the 1989 combined salary of a full position on` d `the year of seniority he is in` grade IS
    CONSIDER `the 1989 table in force on` d
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST t THEN `the cell of the 1989 table` t `the year of seniority he is in` grade

§§ `Examples`

-- §6.1 on 10,000: five classes, entitled, from 1.4.89 is 3%, before then
-- the old 2%; not entitled, nothing. Eight classes from 1.4.89 is 6%;
-- eleven classes keep 4% until 1.9.89; four classes are in no band.
`the 1989 split allowance takes the new rates on their days` MEANS
        `the split allowance under 1989` 5 1 TRUE 10000 (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 5 1989) EQUALS JUST 300
    AND `the split allowance under 1989` 5 1 TRUE 10000 (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 1989) EQUALS JUST 200
    AND `the split allowance under 1989` 5 1 FALSE 10000 (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 5 1989) EQUALS JUST 0
    AND `the split allowance under 1989` 8 1 TRUE 10000 (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 5 1989) EQUALS JUST 600
    AND `the 1989 split rate on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 1989) `eleven classes or more, under 1989` EQUALS 4%
    AND `the 1989 split rate on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 1989) `eleven classes or more, under 1989` EQUALS 7%
    AND `the split allowance under 1989` 4 1 TRUE 10000 (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 5 1989) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the 1989 split allowance takes the new rates on their days`

-- §6.5 on 10,000 from 1.9.89: at 79% 8,900; at 90% the supplement brings
-- her to 10,000; at 91% the completion does too; below 79% nothing is
-- added.
`the 1989 mother teacher's salary at its edges` MEANS
        `a 1989 mother teacher's salary` 0.79 10000 (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 1989) EQUALS 8900
    AND `a 1989 mother teacher's salary` 0.90 10000 (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 1989) EQUALS 10000
    AND `a 1989 mother teacher's salary` 0.91 10000 (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 1989) EQUALS 10000
    AND `a 1989 mother teacher's salary` 0.78 10000 (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 1989) EQUALS 7800
    AND `a 1989 mother teacher's salary` 0.90 10000 (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 8 1989) EQUALS 9000
#ASSERT `the 1989 mother teacher's salary at its edges`

-- The management tables: a seminary principal of 8 classes 36.6%, an
-- elementary first deputy of 12 classes 13.0%, none for an elementary
-- deputy of 11; 13 years of management seniority make the 31.2% the note
-- under the table states for the 14th year on.
`the 1989 management tables read as printed` MEANS
        `the 1989 management allowance percentage` `a teachers' seminary, under 1989` `a principal, under 1989` 8 EQUALS JUST 36.6
    AND `the 1989 management allowance percentage` `an elementary school, under 1989` `a first deputy, under 1989` 12 EQUALS JUST 13.0
    AND `the 1989 management allowance percentage` `an elementary school, under 1989` `a first deputy, under 1989` 11 EQUALS NOTHING
    AND `the 1989 management seniority addition` 14 EQUALS 31.2%
    AND `the 1989 management seniority addition` 30 EQUALS 31.2%
    AND `the 1989 supervision allowance` `a supervisor, under 1989` 11 EQUALS JUST 0.71
    AND `a 1989 college principal's management allowance` 11 EQUALS JUST 0.60
    AND `a 1989 college principal's management allowance` 1 EQUALS JUST 0.40
#ASSERT `the 1989 management tables read as printed`

-- The tables: a B.A. teacher (the third grade column) in his first year
-- earns 848.27 from 1.4.89; the table of 1.6.88 is the one in force on
-- 1.9.88; no table before 1.6.88 or after the period; the cell the scan
-- breaks in the 1.10.88 table's first row stays NOTHING.
`the 1989 tables read as printed` MEANS
        `the 1989 combined salary of a full position on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 5 1989) 1 3 EQUALS JUST 848.27
    AND `the 1989 table in force on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 1988) EQUALS JUST `the 1989 table of 1.6.88`
    AND `the 1989 table in force on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 5 1988) EQUALS NOTHING
    AND `the 1989 table in force on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 4 1990) EQUALS NOTHING
    AND `the cell of the 1989 table` `the 1989 table of 1.10.88` 1 11 EQUALS NOTHING
    AND `the 1989 tables' wage supplement on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 4 1989) EQUALS 10%
#ASSERT `the 1989 tables read as printed`
